---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-signature-pad</code> records a signature drawn with a mouse, finger or pen. Strokes are
  smoothed, a pen draws thicker the harder it presses, and the round buttons undo the last stroke or
  clear the pad. <code>change</code> fires after each stroke with <code>detail.value</code>, the
  signature as a PNG data URL (<code>''</code> while empty).
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 480px;'>
    <wc-signature-pad id='signature-pad-demo' label='Signature' helper-text='Sign above the line'
    ></wc-signature-pad>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#signature-pad-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change: ' + (event.detail.value ? event.detail.value.length + ' characters' : 'empty'));
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Typing instead of drawing</h3>
<p>
  A signature cannot be drawn with a keyboard, so the keyboard button switches the pad to a name field:
  the typed name is drawn on the pad in a script font (<code>--signature-pad-font-family</code>) and
  becomes the value. Each way keeps its own content, and the value follows the one shown. The drawing
  is announced as "Signature, empty" or "Signature, signed".
</p>

<h3>Resizing and exports</h3>
<p>
  Strokes are stored as points, so the pad redraws them sharply at any size and pixel density; they
  scale with the pad's width. <code>toDataURL(type, quality)</code> and
  <code>toBlob(type, quality)</code> export the signature at the pad's size times the device pixel
  ratio, with a transparent background. <code>fromDataURL(url)</code> loads an image onto the pad;
  setting <code>value</code> does the same.
</p>
<p>
  On screen the ink follows the theme (<code>--signature-pad-ink-color</code>, which is light in dark
  mode). Exports always use <code>--signature-pad-export-ink-color</code>, black by default, so a
  signature drawn in dark mode does not come out white.
</p>
